      "message": "Brian, thank you for thorough review, I addressed most of your comments.\n\nBut still, note that this is not meant to be a generic implementation, this is chip/g specific and is residing only in the cr50_stab branch.\n\nThe main branch implementation is not generic, it is for stm32. On top of that it requires an allocation of a buffer to reassemble received packets before writing data to the SPI chip. I don\u0027t see a value in copying by hand some source code which is wrong for the purpose and then hacking it to fit the purpose.\n\nShould there have been a truly generic implementation in common/ in the main branch I would have tried to adopt it, can we agree that I\u0027d do it if such an implementation gets created?",
      "revId": "846394f0cd3e0da15c0e66ac603c887bd92f3133",
