      "writtenOn": "2021-06-24T02:25:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know it\u0027s not common code, but 2/3\u0027s of the file is platform agnostic and the 2 largest changes to the platform agnostic section have to do with the point where the chip select rails are asserted and if there\u0027s a memcpy vs spi transfer when processing each packet.\n\nMy concern is long term maintainability. The more the code bases diverge, the harder it will be to apply a fix between them and the more likely that one version will introduce bugs. Neither implementation is bug free, this CL helped me catch one in the other implementation, but it also would have added quite a few others because so much was rewritten.\n\nIf you\u0027d like, I can implement a version of the original interface sharing 90% of the same platform code with the ability to support either a buffered or non-buffered approach. I am very happy to do this because this will help developers like me maintain support for the protocols. Consistency will make our lives easier in the long run.",
      "parentUuid": "cccd84fa_1ba78154",
      "revId": "846394f0cd3e0da15c0e66ac603c887bd92f3133",
